:1830},{"title":"showFieldMsg\\(String field, String message, String type, Boolean scrollForm\\)","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/api-reference/GlideFormAPINX.md","line":1830},{"title":"Form fields","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/platform-user-interface/c_FormFields.md","line":1933},{"title":"Form fields","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/platform-user-interface/c_FormFields.md","line":2380},{"title":"setValue\\(\\)","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/api-reference/GlideFormAPINX.md","line":2438},{"title":"Configuring read-only security options","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/platform-administration/read-only-option.md","line":2554},{"title":"Display value","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/platform-administration/c_DisplayValues.md","line":2608},{"title":"setReadOnly\\(\\)","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/api-reference/GlideFormAPINX.md","line":2663},{"title":"Service Catalog variable editors","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/servicenow-platform/service-catalog-variable-editor.md","line":2665},{"title":"Annotations","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/platform-administration/configure-form-layout.md","line":2777},{"title":"GlideForm \\(Next Experience\\) - hideAnnotation\\(String name\\)","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/api-reference/GlideFormAPINX.md","line":2779},{"title":"GlideForm \\(Next Experience\\) - toggleAnnotations\\(\\)","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/api-reference/GlideFormAPINX.md","line":2780},{"title":"Annotations","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/platform-administration/configure-form-layout.md","line":3113},{"title":"GlideForm \\(Next Experience\\) - hideAnnotation\\(String name\\)","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/api-reference/GlideFormAPINX.md","line":3115},{"title":"GlideForm \\(Next Experience\\) - showAnnotation\\(String name\\)","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/api-reference/GlideFormAPINX.md","line":3116},{"title":"Client Next Experience API reference","target":"api-client-next","line":3134},{"title":"Catalog client scripts","target":"c_CatalogClientScriptCreation","line":3135},{"title":"Client scripts","target":"client-scripts","line":3136},{"title":"update","target":"r_Update","line":3137}],"metadata":{"title":"GlideForm \\(Next Experience\\) - Client","description":"The GlideForm API provides methods to customize forms in the Next Experience UI Framework.Adds a hidden input with given name and value parameter to the form.Adds a choice to the end of a specified choice list field.Adds an icon on a field's label.Adds an icon on a field's label.Displays the specified error message at the top of the form.Displays a floating form message at the top of the form detail section. The message doesn't cover UI actions.Adds the specified informational message to the top of the form.Displays a high priority message at the top of the form.Displays a low priority message at the top of the form.Displays a moderate priority message at the top of the form.Adds a choice to the end of a specified choice list field.Adds a choice to the list field at the position specified.Displays a message confirming a successful action at the top of the form.Removes all form messages of any type.Removes all choices in a specified choice list field.Removes all form messages of a specified type.Removes all informational and error messages from the top of the form.Removes all options from the specified choice list.Removes any value\\(s\\) from the specified field.Prevents file attachments from being added to the form.Programmatically disables a specific choice in the drop-down field, if the choice exists. No changes are made if the choice is already disabled.Allows file attachments to be added to the form. Shows the paper clip icon.Programmatically enables a specific choice in the drop-down field, if the choice exists. No changes are made if the option is already enabled.Use to draw attention to a field. Flashes the specified color for a specified duration of time in the specified field.Returns the most recent action name, or, for a client script, the sys\\_id of the UI action clicked.Returns a list of all annotations on a form.Returns a form annotation of a given name.Returns a Boolean value for the specified field.Returns an object with properties representing a given field and choice value.Returns the HTML element for the specified field.Returns the decimal value of the specified field.Returns the display value from a form in Service Portal.Returns the HTML element specified by the parameter.Returns the HTML element for the form.Returns the integer value for the specified field.Returns the plain text value of the field label.Returns the available and selected options for a choice or reference field on the form. This method is useful for dynamic forms, catalog variables and variable sets, and integrations needing to inspect or filter field options at runtime.Returns the GlideRecord for a specified field.Returns an array of related list names from the current form.Returns all section names, whether visible or not.Returns an array of the form's sections.Returns the name of the table to which this record belongs.Returns the sys\\_id of the record displayed in the form.Returns the value of the specified form field.Hides all field messages.Hides all field messages of the specified type.Hides an annotation with a given name on the form UI.Hides the error message placed by showErrorBox\\(\\).Hides the first message that appears in the specified field on the current form.Hides the specified related list on the form.Hides all related lists on the form.Returns true if the field is mandatory.Returns true if the record has never been saved.Determines whether the field associated with the passed-in field name is visible on the current form.Registers a custom event listener that detects when any field in the current form is modified by a user.Removes the specified choice from the specified choice list field.Removes the icon from the specified field that matches the specified icon and title.Removes the icon from the specified field that matches the specified icon, title, and color.Removes the specified option from the specified choice list.Saves the record without navigating away \\(update and stay\\).Updates the label of a specific choice in the drop-down field.Makes the specified field available or unavailable.Displays or hides a specified field on the form.Sets the plain text value of the specified field label.Makes the specified field mandatory.Makes the specified field read-only or editable.Shows or hides a specified section in the form.Sets the value of a specified form field to the specified value or the value of a specified display value in a reference record.Makes a Service Catalog variable editor read only.Displays or hides the specified field.Shows an annotation with a given name on the form UI.Displays an error message under the specified form field \\(either a control object or the name of the field\\). If the control or field is currently off the screen, the form automatically scrolls to the control or field.Displays an error message under the specified form field \\(either a control object or the name of the field\\). If the control or field is currently off the screen and the scrollForm parameter is true, the form scrolls to the control or field.Displays a message under the specified form field \\(either a control object or the name of the field\\). If the control or field is off the screen, the method automatically scrolls the form to that field.Displays a message under the specified form field \\(either a control object or the name of the field\\). If the control or field is currently off the screen and scrollForm is true, the method scrolls the form to that field.Displays the specified related list on the form.Displays all the form's related lists.Saves the record.Performs the specified UI action.Hides or shows all annotations on the form.","locale":"en-US","canonical_url":"https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/api-reference/GlideFormAPINX.html","release":"australia","product":"API Reference","classification":"api-reference","topic_type":"concept","last_updated":"2026-03-12","reading_time_minutes":46,"breadcrumb":["Client Next Experience API reference","API reference","API implementation and reference"],"tags":["#api-reference","#type-concept"]},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[[47,54],[58,67],[83,85],[195,197],[319,321],[337,339],[405,424],[464,475],[483,499],[501,519],[521,539],[541,559],[561,577],[579,598],[600,618],[620,642],[644,658],[660,707],[709,725],[727,741],[743,838],[856,905],[913,981],[983,999],[1004,1032],[1034,1072],[1094,1143],[1145,1183],[1193,1232],[1234,1276],[1280,1312],[1316,1339],[1354,1410],[1415,1448],[1450,1476],[1478,1483],[1513,1517],[1525,1571],[1585,1591],[1619,1630],[1646,1652],[1666,1671],[1689,1693],[1697,1718],[1808,1810],[1834,1838],[1888,1899],[1955,1961],[1993,2000],[2043,2052],[2067,2069],[2087,2103],[2122,2124],[2139,2141],[2232,2238],[2340,2352],[2369,2374],[2486,2496],[2617,2619],[2623,2643],[2647,2649],[2653,2655],[2703,2705],[2759,2771],[2813,2815],[2963,2965],[3051,3053],[3128,3130]],"key":"ServiceNowOfficialDocs/api-reference/GlideFormAPINX.md"},
